        "content": "# Feature: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Feature ID\n`yaml-validator-command`\n\n## Summary\nAdd a simple YAML validator command to the project that validates YAML syntax without adding any new dependencies. Uses a hand-written parser leveraging only Bun/TypeScript built-ins.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement | Priority |\n|----|-------------|----------|\n| FR-1 | Provide a `validateYaml(input: string)` function that checks whether a string is valid YAML | Must |\n| FR-2 | Return a structured result object with `valid: boolean` and optional `error: string` fields | Must |\n| FR-3 | Support basic YAML constructs: key-value pairs, nested objects (indentation-based), arrays (dash prefix), strings, numbers, booleans, null | Must |\n| FR-4 | Detect common YAML syntax errors: bad indentation, duplicate keys, invalid characters, unclosed quotes | Must |\n| FR-5 | Provide a CLI entry point `src/validate-yaml.ts` that reads a file path from argv and prints validation results | Must |\n| FR-6 | Add a `validate` script to package.json: `bun run src/validate-yaml.ts` | Should |\n\n### Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement | Priority |\n|----|-------------|----------|\n| NFR-1 | Zero new dependencies — use only Bun built-ins and hand-written TypeScript | Must |\n| NFR-2 | Follow existing project patterns: camelCase functions, PascalCase types, kebab-case files | Must |\n| NFR-3 | Co-located tests in `src/yaml-validator.test.ts` using Bun's test runner | Must |\n| NFR-4 | TypeScript strict mode compatible | Must |\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n| ID | Criteria |\n|----|----------|\n| AC-1 | `validateYaml('name: John')` returns `{ valid: true }` |\n| AC-2 | `validateYaml('name: : invalid')` returns `{ valid: false, error: \"...\" }` |\n| AC-3 | Validates nested YAML with proper indentation |\n| AC-4 | Validates YAML arrays (dash-prefixed lists) |\n| AC-5 | CLI prints \"Valid YAML\" or error details to stdout |\n| AC-6 | All tests pass with `bun test` |\n| AC-7 | No new entries in package.json dependencies or devDependencies (except @types/bun) |\n\n## Constraints\n- No external YAML parsing libraries (js-yaml, yaml, etc.)\n- Must work with Bun runtime\n- Must not break existing functionality\n"
