        "content": "# Tasks: yaml-validator-command\n\n## Implementation Tasks\n\n### T1: Create YAML validator core module\n- **Status**: done\n- **Complexity**: medium\n- **Files**: `src/yaml-validator.ts`\n- **Description**: Implement the `YamlValidationResult` interface and `validateYaml()` function with line-by-line YAML structural validation. Must handle: key-value pairs, nested objects via indentation, arrays (dash prefix), comments, blank lines, strings/numbers/booleans/null values. Detect errors: tab indentation, inconsistent indentation, duplicate keys at same level, unclosed quotes, invalid syntax lines.\n- **Acceptance**: Function correctly validates well-formed YAML and returns descriptive errors with line numbers for malformed input.\n- **Summary**: Implemented `YamlValidationResult` interface and `validateYaml()` function in `src/yaml-validator.ts`. Uses line-by-line structural validation with indentation stack tracking, duplicate key detection per indentation level, unclosed quote detection, and tab/inconsistent indentation error reporting. Handles key-value pairs, nested objects, arrays, comments, document markers, booleans, nulls, and numbers. Returns `{ valid: true }` or `{ valid: false, error, line }`.\n\n### T2: Create YAML validator unit tests\n- **Status**: done\n- **Complexity**: medium\n- **Files**: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`\n- **Description**: Write comprehensive unit tests for `validateYaml()` covering: valid simple key-value, valid nested objects, valid arrays, valid mixed structures, invalid tab indentation, invalid inconsistent indentation, invalid duplicate keys, invalid unclosed quotes, invalid malformed syntax, empty input edge case, multiline strings, boolean/null/number values.\n- **Acceptance**: All tests pass with `bun test`. Coverage of all acceptance criteria from requirements.\n- **Summary**: Created 24 tests across 3 describe blocks: valid YAML (14 tests: simple kv, multiple kv, nested, arrays, array of objects, booleans, nulls, numbers, quoted strings, comments, blank lines, empty input, whitespace-only, document markers, mixed structure), invalid YAML (7 tests: tabs, duplicate keys, unclosed quotes ×2, unexpected colon, inconsistent indentation, line numbers), result structure (2 tests). All passing.\n\n### T3: Create CLI entry point and package.json script\n- **Status**: done\n- **Complexity**: simple\n- **Files**: `src/validate-yaml.ts`, `package.json`\n- **Description**: Create CLI entry point that reads a file path from `process.argv[2]`, reads the file using `Bun.file()`, calls `validateYaml()`, and prints \"Valid YAML\" or error details. Add `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` script to package.json. Handle missing file argument with usage message and exit code 1.\n- **Acceptance**: `bun run validate test.yaml` validates a YAML file and prints results. Missing arg shows usage.\n- **Summary**: Created `src/validate-yaml.ts` CLI that reads file path from argv, checks file existence via `Bun.file().exists()`, reads content, calls `validateYaml()`, prints \"Valid YAML\" or error with line number, exits with code 1 on error. Added `\"validate\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` script to package.json.\n\n## Documentation Tasks\n\n(None — no external documentation required for this feature)\n"
