        "file_path": "/private/tmp/rp1-evals/067c306c/workspace/.rp1/work/features/yaml-validator-command/design.md",
        "content": "# Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Feature ID\nyaml-validator-command\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Overview\nA simple YAML validator built as a pure-function module with a thin CLI wrapper. No new dependencies — uses string parsing with Bun built-in file I/O.\n\n### Component Diagram\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── yaml-validator.ts      # Core validation logic (pure functions)\n├── yaml-validator.test.ts # Unit tests for validator\n└── validate-yaml.ts       # CLI entry point\n```\n\n### Module Design\n\n#### `src/yaml-validator.ts` — Core Validator\n\n**Types:**\n```typescript\ninterface ValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: string[];\n}\n```\n\n**Exported Functions:**\n- `validateYaml(input: string): ValidationResult` — Main entry point. Runs all checks and aggregates errors.\n\n**Internal Functions:**\n- `checkIndentation(lines: string[]): string[]` — Validates consistent indentation (spaces only, consistent width, proper nesting).\n- `checkQuotes(lines: string[]): string[]` — Detects unclosed single/double quotes.\n- `checkDuplicateKeys(lines: string[]): string[]` — Detects duplicate keys at the same indentation level.\n- `checkStructure(lines: string[]): string[]` — Validates basic YAML key-value structure (colon-separated, proper list markers).\n\n**Validation Rules:**\n1. No tabs for indentation (YAML forbids tabs).\n2. Consistent indentation width within a document.\n3. All opened quotes must be closed on the same line.\n4. No duplicate keys at the same indentation level.\n5. Lines with content should be valid key-value pairs, list items, or comments.\n\n#### `src/validate-yaml.ts` — CLI Entry Point\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Read file path from `process.argv[2]`.\n2. If no path provided, print usage and exit(1).\n3. Read file using `Bun.file(path).text()`.\n4. Call `validateYaml(content)`.\n5. If valid: print \"✓ Valid YAML\" to stdout, exit(0).\n6. If invalid: print each error prefixed with line info, exit(1).\n7. On file read error: print error message, exit(1).\n\n#### `package.json` Change\n\nAdd script:\n```json\n\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"\n```\n\n### Testing Strategy\n\nTest file: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`\n\n**Test Cases:**\n1. Valid simple key-value YAML → `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n2. Valid nested YAML → `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n3. Valid YAML with comments → `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n4. Valid YAML with list items → `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n5. Tab indentation → error detected\n6. Inconsistent indentation → error detected\n7. Unclosed quotes → error detected\n8. Duplicate keys → error detected\n9. Empty input → `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`\n\n### Design Decisions\n\n1. **No external YAML parser**: Requirement explicitly states no new deps. We implement a basic structural validator, not a full parser.\n2. **Line-by-line analysis**: Simple approach sufficient for basic validation. Each check function processes lines independently.\n3. **Aggregated errors**: All checks run and errors are collected, giving users the full picture rather than failing at first error.\n4. **Pure functions**: Core logic is testable without filesystem access. CLI wrapper is a thin layer.\n\n### Flagged Hypotheses\nNone — straightforward implementation with no ambiguous design choices.\n"
